From @potrh @end|ng |rom gm@||@com  Thu Jul 28 20:10:08 2022
From: @potrh @end|ng |rom gm@||@com (Tom Callaway)
Date: Thu, 28 Jul 2022 14:10:08 -0400
Subject: [R-sig-Fedora] Rawhide side tag for R 4.2.1 builds
Message-ID: <CACp8Zr+YfsGA5z6pfnfuvKC9TrgfaTUODWKyNmOVv-nAqr=xSQ@mail.gmail.com>

Hi folks, I've created a side tag in rawhide for R 4.2.1 builds. Please
keep in mind that because this takes rawhide from R 4.1 to R 4.2, all R
packages (and R dependent packages) will need to be rebuilt into this side
tag. Once that is done, we can merge the builds from the side tag back into
rawhide.

Use 'fedpkg build --target=f37-build-side-55653' to use it.
Use 'koji wait-repo f37-build-side-55653' to wait for the build repo to be
generated.

I've built R-4.2.1-1.fc37, rpy-3.5.3-1.fc37, and rkward-0.7.4-1.fc37 into
that tag, so please feel free to start rebuilding any R dependent packages
that you maintain in that tag.

If you need the raw R-4.2.1 packages for local testing, they're here:
https://koji.fedoraproject.org/koji/taskinfo?taskID=90194354

I plan on starting to work my way through everything in Fedora as time
permits, but I'm not sure when exactly that will happen. :(

Any help others can provide in rebuilding dependencies is appreciated. :)

~spot

